From 8188d172efc7b4ca0b598eda3decac70c920ef36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anuj Gupta <anuj20.g@samsung.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 15:33:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 08/17] nvme-pci: fix map and sgt leak on the seg_shift
 driver-bug path

nvme_dma_buf_io_map(), added by patch 11 of "Add dmabuf read/write via
io_uring", asserts that every DMA segment in the mapping is at least
page-sized:

	if (WARN_ON_ONCE(seg_shift < NVME_CTRL_PAGE_SHIFT))
		return ERR_PTR(-EFAULT);

Every other error in this function goes through the err: label, which
unmaps the attachment and frees map. This one returns directly instead,
so it leaks the nvme_dmabuf_map allocation and, more importantly, leaves
the scatter-gather table mapped via dma_buf_map_attachment() with
nothing left holding a reference to unmap it -- a real DMA mapping leak,
not just memory.

Route it through the existing err: label like every other failure in
this function.

Signed-off-by: Anuj Gupta <anuj20.g@samsung.com>
---
 drivers/nvme/host/pci.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c b/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c
index 67e26d6e8f25..868524ca3575 100644
--- a/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c
@@ -2617,8 +2617,10 @@ static struct dma_buf_io_map *nvme_dma_buf_io_map(struct dma_buf_io_ctx *ctx)
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (WARN_ON_ONCE(seg_shift < NVME_CTRL_PAGE_SHIFT))
-		return ERR_PTR(-EFAULT);
+	if (WARN_ON_ONCE(seg_shift < NVME_CTRL_PAGE_SHIFT)) {
+		ret = -EFAULT;
+		goto err;
+	}
 
 	ret = dma_buf_io_init_map(ctx, &map->base);
 	if (ret)
-- 
